  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1212 PM CDT Sat Aug 8 2026\n\nSome modeling suggests the presence of a weak area of low\npressure slipping in the wake of the surface ridge's eastward\ndeparture may allow a small chance of a shower/storm across the\narea, particularly the southeast. We'll leave that mention in\nthere as this morning's CAMs struggle with a fixed solution but\nall produce some minimal noise output with respect to pcpn into\nthis early evening.\n\nWarm sectoring takes over thereafter, as the broader upper high\nbuilds over the Gulf thru mid week. The resultant warm advection\nfetch manifests here with higher temps, higher dew points, and \npushing headline HI's. While considering a duration Advisory for\nSunday-Wednesday, the new 12Z NBM's numbers have returned more \nmarginal around the century mark for Sunday, and convective \nchances increase Wednesday, so we're going to punt and focus on \nthe Monday-Tuesday timing of best heat for headlines in \npotential future packages, should the numbers hold and warrant; \nfor now we're mainly in the 100-105 range Monday-Tuesday.\n\nStorm chances really climb toward the week's end, as a sharper\nlong wave trof digs across the Great Lakes and pushes a cold\nfront toward the Ohio Valley. Thursday looks to be the best such\nchance for storms, and any potential for stronger storms look \nbest Thursday as well.",
